  "change_kinds": [
    {
      "id": "skills",
      "name": "What the assistant knows how to do (skills)",
      "who": "the person running the assistant",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 2,
      "evidence": "The product drafts skills: /learn stages a pending proposal for the person to apply (src/skills/workshop/learn-prompt.ts:23-34), and the experience review writes skills from observed runs (experience-review.ts). People also apply, reject or quarantine proposals (src/cli/skills-cli.ts:877-1135). Undo: skill collections are backed up and restored or rolled back by revision hash (src/skills/workshop/collection-backup.ts, collection-restore.ts, collection-rollback.ts). Reach 2, not 3: DEL-04 is 2, and nothing checks and stages a skill change end to end for approval by default.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "reach_name": "Drafted"
    },
    {
      "id": "memory-persona",
      "name": "What the assistant remembers and how it presents itself",
      "who": "the person running the assistant",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 0,
      "evidence": "Memory and persona files (MEMORY.md, SOUL.md, AGENTS.md in the workspace) change in chat and through dreaming, which is on by default (docs/concepts/dreaming.md). No supported undo: the workspace is only `git init`-ed at creation and never committed (src/agents/workspace.ts:682-708); dreaming keeps MEMORY.md preimages in plugin state but offers no restore command; `memory forget` deletes by source session, it does not revert (docs/cli/memory.md). Reach 0 because the path has no undo. Undo rule used in this field test: a kind has undo when the product keeps the earlier version, or when the change is a selection, toggle or add-and-remove that the same supported path reverses exactly; free-text or multi-field edits with no kept version have none.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Engineers only"
    },
    {
      "id": "models-channels",
      "name": "Which models, providers and chat channels it uses",
      "who": "the person running the assistant",
      "main": true,
      "reach": 2,
      "evidence": "Models and providers are selected, and channels connected and disconnected, through onboarding, the Control UI and the validated `openclaw config set|unset` (src/cli/config-cli.ts:330-479). The system agent drafts each such change as a pending proposal that the person approves before it applies, then checks it with the config validator (src/system-agent/assistant-prompts.ts:159-161, src/agents/tools/system-agent-tool.ts). Undo: re-selecting the previous model or disconnecting the channel through the same path; wider configuration edits keep no operator-visible earlier version (five rotating backups serve only automatic recovery, src/config/backup-rotation.ts). Reach 2 rests on DEL-04 2. Undo rule used in this field test: a kind has undo when the product keeps the earlier version, or when the change is a selection, toggle or add-and-remove that the same supported path reverses exactly; free-text or multi-field edits with no kept version have none.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Drafted"
    },
    {
      "id": "tool-permissions",
      "name": "What the assistant may do and who may instruct it",
      "who": "the person running the assistant",
      "main": false,
      "reach": 1,
      "evidence": "Exec allowlist entries are added and removed with `openclaw approvals` and exec policy commands (src/cli/exec-approvals-cli.ts, exec-policy-cli.ts), and senders are paired and revoked with `openclaw pairing` (src/pairing). Undo is removing the entry or revoking the pairing; there is no history of earlier policy versions (GOV-05 inventory: configuration 2). Undo rule used in this field test: a kind has undo when the product keeps the earlier version, or when the change is a selection, toggle or add-and-remove that the same supported path reverses exactly; free-text or multi-field edits with no kept version have none.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Self-serve"
    },
    {
      "id": "scheduled-jobs",
      "name": "Scheduled and recurring tasks",
      "who": "the person running the assistant",
      "main": false,
      "reach": 1,
      "evidence": "Jobs are created, edited, paused and removed through `openclaw automations add|edit|remove` and the agent's cron tool (docs/cli/cron.md, src/agents/tools/cron-tool.ts), with no deploy. Undo is by disabling or removing the job; edits keep no earlier version (src/cron/config-revision.ts is a concurrency token only), so an edit is undone only by editing it back.",
      "confidence": "low",
      "reach_name": "Self-serve"
    },
    {
      "id": "plugins",
      "name": "Add-ons for new channels, tools and providers",
      "who": "the person running the assistant",
      "main": false,
      "reach": 2,
      "evidence": "People install curated plugins from ClawHub, bundled or official sources and remove them with uninstall (docs/plugins/manage-plugins.md). The agent can write a plugin, pack it with `openclaw plugins pack`, and the system agent proposes activating that exact archive for the person to approve (src/system-agent/plugin-artifact.ts, src/agents/tools/system-agent-tool.ts). Undo is plugin_uninstall. Reach 2 rests on DEL-04 2.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "reach_name": "Drafted"
    }
